   "question": "<ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li><p>Express as partial fractions</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{2x^2+3x+6}{(x+1)(x^2+4)}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li><li><p>Hence, show that</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\int_0^2\\frac{2x^2+3x+6}{(x+1)(x^2+4)}\\,\\mathrm dx=\\ln\\left(a\\sqrt2\\right)+b\\pi\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> are constants to be determined.</p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol>",
